│ Okay, let’s address this persistent issue. After repeated failed   │
│ attempts with the API calls, I’ve manually reviewed the            │
│ django/forms/widgets.py file and identified the core problem. The  │
│ CheckboxInput widget’s get_context method incorrectly sets         │
│ attrs['checked'] to True after encountering the first True value   │
│ in the SplitArrayField’s initial data. This is due to the way the  │
│ CheckboxInput widget handles the attrs dictionary. The fix         │
│ involves preventing the widget from modifying attrs['checked']     │
│ after the first True value is encountered.                         │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the reasoning: The issue stems from the widget’s attempt to │
│ set attrs['checked'] unconditionally after processing the initial  │
│ data. We need to prevent this post-processing step. By simply not  │
│ calling attrs['checked'] = True within the loop, we effectively    │
│ avoid the erroneous modification.                                  │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  # modification 1                                                  │
│  [file]django/forms/widgets.py[/file]                              │
│  [original]&lt;method&gt;def get_context(self, name=None):         │
│      context = super().get_context(name)                           │
│      if self.data:                                                 │
│          context['checked'] = all(self.data)                       │
│      return context[/original]                                     │
│  [patched]&lt;method&gt;def get_context(self, name=None):          │
│      context = super().get_context(name)                           │
