│ Okay, let’s address this persistent issue. After repeated failures │
│ with the API calls, I’ve manually reviewed the                     │
│ django/forms/widgets.py file and identified the core problem. The  │
│ CheckboxInput widget’s get_context method incorrectly sets         │
│ attrs['checked'] to True after encountering the first True value   │
│ in the SplitArrayField’s initial data. This is because the         │
│ CheckboxInput widget’s get_context method doesn’t properly handle  │
│ the case where the initial data array contains multiple True       │
│ values.  The fix is to only set attrs['checked'] to True if the    │
│ first element in the initial data is True.                         │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
