│ Okay, I’ve analyzed the retrieved code and understand the issue.   │
│ The CheckboxInput widget incorrectly sets attrs['checked'] to True │
│ after encountering the first True value in the SplitArrayField’s   │
│ boolean data. This is because the get_context() method doesn’t     │
│ properly reset the attrs['checked'] state when encountering a      │
│ False value. The fix involves ensuring that attrs['checked'] is    │
│ only set to True when the corresponding data is actually True.     │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
