│ Okay, let’s address this issue. Based on the provided context and  │
│ the repeated errors with API calls, the core problem is that the   │
│ CheckboxInput widget incorrectly modifies the attrs dictionary     │
│ passed to its get_context method, leading to all subsequent        │
│ checkboxes being checked even if the underlying data is false. The │
│ fix involves preventing the attrs['checked'] = True assignment     │
│ within get_context when the initial data is false.                 │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃                         modification 1                         ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file][original]django/forms/widgets.py[/original]                │
│  [patched]                                                         │
│  def get_context(self, name=None):                                 │
│      context = super().get_context(name)                           │
│      if name == 'checked' and self.data and self.data[0]:          │
│          context['checked'] = True                                 │
│      return context                                                │
│  [/patched]                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃                         modification 2                         ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
