│  class SplitArrayField(Field):                                     │
│      def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):                          │
│          super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)                         │
│      [/patched]                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The first modification directly addresses the issue within the     │
│ CheckboxInput.get_context() method. It adds a conditional check:   │
│ if name == 'checked' and self.data and self.data[0]:. This ensures │
│ that the attrs['checked'] = True assignment only happens if the    │
│ SplitArrayField’s data is not empty and the first element of the   │
│ data is true. This prevents the widget from incorrectly setting    │
│ the checked state when the initial data is false.                  │
│                                                                    │
│ The second modification is a minor adjustment to the               │
│ SplitArrayField class. It removes the unnecessary __init__ method, │
│ as it doesn’t contribute to the core functionality of the field    │
│ and simplifies the code. This ensures that the SplitArrayField     │
│ doesn't inadvertently influence the checkbox's state.              │
│                                                                    │
│ This patch should resolve the described bug by preventing the      │
│ incorrect setting of the attrs['checked'] attribute when the       │
│ initial data is false, thus ensuring that checkboxes are only      │
│ checked when the corresponding data is true.                       │
